Algorithm for ChangeKey:

Step 1: Check whether the given index is valid in the heap.
Step 2: If the index is outside the heap range, stop the process.
Step 3: Store the old value present at the given index.
Step 4: Replace the value at that index with the new value.
Step 5: Compare the old value with the new value.
Step 6: If the new value is smaller than the old value, apply the heapify process from that index to restore the Max Heap property downward.
Step 7: If the new value is greater than the old value, move the element upward in the heap.
Step 8: Compare the current element with its parent node.
Step 9: If the current element is greater than the parent, swap them.
Step 10: Continue moving the element upward until the Max Heap property is satisfied or the root is reached.

Time Complexity: O(log n)
Space Complexity: O(1)



